  "body": "`upstream/main` (51979785 and later, through 7f0928fe) does not compile: `crates/motion/src/machining2d/trochoid_slot.rs` has 7 errors (E0308/E0609) at lines 231-239.\n\n**Cause:** two merged PRs collided semantically.\n- #783 (motion onto Stock) made `quality::measure` return `Result<PathQuality, StockError>`.\n- The trochoidal slot work (#563, and #778 on top of it) calls `measure(...)` and reads `q.max_deg` / `q.max_at` on the result directly.\nEach PR built on its own; the merge of both does not.\n\n**Effect:** every crate that depends on camcraft-motion (app, ui, cli) fails to build on main. Every PR gate is red until this is fixed.\n\n**Fix:** map the `measure` error into the generator's named `GenError` (the same \"trochoidal slot: measuring stock: …\" wording the `stock()` closure already uses), so a stock failure refuses by name.\n\nDone means: main builds; motion's trochoid tests and the app suites pass.\n",
